  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "{\"representation\":\"living-reconstruction\",\"scope\":\"Whole animal preserving the original genus-level target: long lightly built hindlimbs and extended narrow neck. Concrete species reference D.elderae, not old D.altus label or African Dysalotosaurus.\",\"scientific_limits\":{\"en\":\"Original living reconstruction, not scan. Carnegie CM3392 mount includes substantial casts and sculpted restoration;2007 account reports only35% original bones and about25% newly sculpted. Head is checked against NPS adult skull cast; soft tissue, posture and missing parts remain inferred. Three metres is an approximate museum-mount display scale, not complete fossil measurement.\",\"zh\":\"完整活体美术复原，非扫描。Carnegie CM3392装架含大量翻模与雕塑补配，2007馆方说明原骨约35%、约25%新塑。头部另核NPS成年头骨翻模；软组织、姿态及缺失部分属推断。3米为约定展件尺度，非完整化石实测。\"},\"inventory_ordinal\":368,\"name\":{\"en\":\"Dryosaurus\",\"zh\":\"橡树龙\"},\"taxon\":\"Dryosaurus elderae\",\"classification\":\"Dinosauria, Ornithischia, Ornithopoda, Dryosauridae\",\"scale\":{\"total_length_m\":3.0,\"basis\":\"Carnegie2007 describes roughly10-foot mount; current NPS gives broad8-14foot estimates and2.4m smaller adult example. Three metres is approximate within that range.\"},\"diagnostic_targets\":[\"Slender extended neck joins small tapered beaked head to a moderately deep torso.\",\"Long lightly built hindlimbs and narrow distal legs, distinct from stocky adult sauropodomorphs.\",\"Short five-fingered forelimbs held free, no Iguanodon thumb spike.\",\"Long tapering tail balances bipedal body; no horns, large predator teeth or armour.\",\"Retain genuine neck/leg proportions versus compact short-necked Hypsilophodon, not size-only distinction.\"],\"specimen_basis\":\"Actual Carnegie mounted skeleton side photograph and official frontal photo inspected; NPS adult skull cast image with inch scale inspected. Current NPS species name D.elderae used, original genus scope preserved.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：{\"representation\":\"living-reconstruction\",\"scope\":\"Whole animal preserving the original genus-level target: long lightly built hindlimbs and extended narrow neck. Concrete species reference D.elderae, not old D.altus label or African Dysalotosaurus.\",\"scientific_limits\":{\"en\":\"Original living reconstruction, not scan. Carnegie CM3392 mount includes substantial casts and sculpted restoration;2007 account reports only35% original bones and about25% newly sculpted. Head is checked against NPS adult skull cast; soft tissue, posture and missing parts remain inferred. Three metres is an approximate museum-mount display scale, not complete fossil measurement.\",\"zh\":\"完整活体美术复原，非扫描。Carnegie CM3392装架含大量翻模与雕塑补配，2007馆方说明原骨约35%、约25%新塑。头部另核NPS成年头骨翻模；软组织、姿态及缺失部分属推断。3米为约定展件尺度，非完整化石实测。\"},\"inventory_ordinal\":368,\"name\":{\"en\":\"Dryosaurus\",\"zh\":\"橡树龙\"},\"taxon\":\"Dryosaurus elderae\",\"classification\":\"Dinosauria, Ornithischia, Ornithopoda, Dryosauridae\",\"scale\":{\"total_length_m\":3.0,\"basis\":\"Carnegie2007 describes roughly10-foot mount; current NPS gives broad8-14foot estimates and2.4m smaller adult example. Three metres is approximate within that range.\"},\"diagnostic_targets\":[\"Slender extended neck joins small tapered beaked head to a moderately deep torso.\",\"Long lightly built hindlimbs and narrow distal legs, distinct from stocky adult sauropodomorphs.\",\"Short five-fingered forelimbs held free, no Iguanodon thumb spike.\",\"Long tapering tail balances bipedal body; no horns, large predator teeth or armour.\",\"Retain genuine neck/leg proportions versus compact short-necked Hypsilophodon, not size-only distinction.\"],\"specimen_basis\":\"Actual Carnegie mounted skeleton side photograph and official frontal photo inspected; NPS adult skull cast image with inch scale inspected. Current NPS species name D.elderae used, original genus scope preserved.\"}"
  },
